Free the SPU's output buffer when the SPU is destroyed

SPU::InitOutput() mallocs OutputBuffer and nothing ever frees it, so every
destroyed NDS leaves its sound buffer behind. Retro Pal builds a new NDS for
every game it opens, so each game launch leaked one. The destructor now frees it.

Upstream commit 0638e5bc ("Fix SPU output buffer leak", 2026-05-05), taken as is.
It changes nothing an emulated frame produces: checked with Tools/nds-bench,
identical pictures and sound on every frame.

Applied at build time by Vendor/melonds-ios/build.sh. It goes away with the
submodule bump that contains the upstream commit.

diff --git a/src/SPU.cpp b/src/SPU.cpp
index 1ae6abda..e1d49f96 100644
--- a/src/SPU.cpp
+++ b/src/SPU.cpp
@@ -226,6 +226,12 @@ SPU::SPU(melonDS::NDS& nds, AudioBitDepth bitdepth, AudioInterpolation interpola
 
 SPU::~SPU()
 {
+    if (OutputBuffer != nullptr)
+    {
+        free(OutputBuffer);
+        OutputBuffer = nullptr;
+    }
+
     Platform::Mutex_Free(AudioLock);
     AudioLock = nullptr;
     blip_delete(BlipLeft);
